/S /H2
/P 271 0 R
/T (Safety precautions)
/E (Safety precautions)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
3221 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 271 0 R
/E (The frameless motor rotors contain high-energy rare-earth magnets that produce strong magnetic fields. Therefore, anyone with active implants, such as pacemakers, should keep a safe distance from the rotors of these motors.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
3222 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 271 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
3223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 271 0 R
/E (Strong magnetic fields produced by the rotor magnets may affect or damage electronic devices & measuring equipment. Rotors should not be placed near computer disks, computers, monitors, credit cards, etc.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
3224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 271 0 R
/T (Handling & Storage)
/E (Handling & Storage)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
3225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 271 0 R
/E (Correct handling & storage of motor components is very important. It is recommended that stators & rotors be stored in their original packaging until installation is required. Special care must be taken when handling stator assemblies, as damage to the coil insulation and lead wires can result in electrical shorts and possible electrical shocks. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
3226 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 271 0 R
/E (Precautions should also be taken when handling the rotor assembly, as strong magnetic forces are present. The magnets on the rotor are brittle & prone to cracking, chipping, or even shattering on impact. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
3227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 271 0 R
/E (Do not pull on the phase cables, while stripping the cables, a proper cable stripping tool that does not pull on the cable must be used.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
3228 0 obj
<<
