3281 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 273 0 R
/T (The most space efficient option is to bond the parts using a low viscosity adhesive or retaining compound with sufficient temperature range \(such as Loctite 638\). The mating surfaces should be clean & dry prior to assembly & the parts needs to be held in position during the initial cure. It should be noted that disassembly is not possible with this retention method. )
/E (The most space efficient option is to bond the parts using a low viscosity adhesive or retaining compound with sufficient temperature range \(such as Loctite 638\). The mating surfaces should be clean & dry prior to assembly & the parts needs to be held in position during the initial cure. It should be noted that disassembly is not possible with this retention method. )
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
