<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 274 0 R
/T (Stator alignment options: 1. Alignment with the stator housing 2. In-situ alignment with spacers)
/E (Stator alignment options: 1. Alignment with the stator housing 2. In-situ alignment with spacers)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
3310 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 274 0 R
/T (Alignment through the housing is achieved by a clearance fit between the stator sleeve and the housing. In this case the housing mating surface ID should be dimensioned equal to the Stator sleeve OD with a H8 tolerance or tighter. The housing mating surface should be concentric to the rotor carrier rotation axis to within 0.1mm in the final assembly.)
/E (Alignment through the housing is achieved by a clearance fit between the stator sleeve and the housing. In this case the housing mating surface ID should be dimensioned equal to the Stator sleeve OD with a H8 tolerance or tighter. The housing mating surface should be concentric to the rotor carrier rotation axis to within 0.1mm in the final assembly.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
3311 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 274 0 R
/T (In situ alignment is achieved by first assembling the rotor, then bonding the stator into the housing while using spacers between the stator & rotor to ensure the correct airgap. In this case there should be a minimal stator sleeve to housing gap of 0.1mm \(minimal, not nominal\). This method of assembly, tough more process demanding, reduces the need for high precision on the housing ID & general assembly tolerances. Note that the requirement for rotor carrier tolerances still apply.)
/E (In situ alignment is achieved by first assembling the rotor, then bonding the stator into the housing while using spacers between the stator & rotor to ensure the correct airgap. In this case there should be a minimal stator sleeve to housing gap of 0.1mm \(minimal, not nominal\). This method of assembly, tough more process demanding, reduces the need for high precision on the housing ID & general assembly tolerances. Note that the requirement for rotor carrier tolerances still apply.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
