18837 0 obj
<<
/Title (Alignment through the housing is achieved by a clearance fit between the stator sleeve and the housing. In this case the housing mating surface ID should be dimensioned equal to the Stator sleeve OD with a H8 tolerance or tighter. The housing mating surface should be concentric to the rotor carrier rotation axis to within 0.1mm in the final assembly.)
/Dest [41 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 18779 0 R
/Prev 18807 0 R
/Next 18838 0 R
>>
endobj
18838 0 obj
<<
/Title (In situ alignment is achieved by first assembling the rotor, then bonding the stator into the housing while using spacers between the stator & rotor to ensure the correct airgap. In this case there should be a minimal stator sleeve to housing gap of 0.1mm \(minimal, not nominal\). This method of assembly, tough more process demanding, reduces the need for high precision on the housing ID & general assembly tolerances. Note that the requirement for rotor carrier tolerances still apply.)
/Dest [41 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 18779 0 R
/Prev 18837 0 R
/First 18866 0 R
/Last 18867 0 R
/Count -3
/Next 18808 0 R
>>
endobj
